-- title:
--   Compatible pairs $(\alpha,g)$ with $\alpha\theta(q)=\theta'(\beta_g q)\alpha$
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be prime, $Q$ a finite group, $\theta,\theta':Q\to\mathrm{GL}(a,p)$ representations on $M=M'=\mathbb F_p^a$, $\Gamma\le\mathrm{Sym}(\Omega)$ the group generated by given permutations, and $\beta:\Gamma\to\mathrm{Aut}(Q)$ a homomorphism, $\beta_g=\beta(g)$. The **compatible pairs** are
--   $$
--   \{(\alpha,g)\in\mathrm{GL}(a,p)\times\Gamma:\ \alpha\,\theta(q)=\theta'(\beta_g q)\,\alpha\ \text{ for all }q\in Q\},\tag{9.2}
--   $$
--   and the **source stabilizer** is the set of compatible pairs for $(\theta,\theta)$, a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}(a,p)\times\Gamma$. When nonempty, the compatible pairs form a left coset of the source stabilizer.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Bases of $M$ and $M'$ are fixed, so $\mathrm{Iso}_{\mathbb F_p}(M,M')$ is $\mathrm{GL}(a,p)$; $\Omega=\{0,\dots,k-1\}$. The homomorphism $\beta$ need not be injective.
-- source:
--   Qiao, Zhang, Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Definition 27, (9.2), p.93 (PDF p.97)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace GroupIsoPoly

/-- The permutation group `Γ = ⟨gens⟩ ≤ Sym(Ω)`, `Ω = Fin k`. -/
def gammaOf {k s : ℕ} (gens : Fin s → Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) : Subgroup (Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) :=
  Subgroup.closure (Set.range gens)

/-- **Compatible pairs** (9.2) of module action compatibility.

Qiao, Zhang, *Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order*, preprint,
Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Definition 27, p.93 (PDF p.97): "Let p be prime, let Q
be a finite table group, and let M, M′ be a-dimensional Fp-spaces with representations θ : Q → GL(M)
and θ′ : Q → GL(M′) given on a specified generating set of Q. Also given are generators of
Γ ≤ Sym(Ω) and their images under β : Γ → Aut(Q). Write βg = β(g). The call M(Q, θ, θ′; Γ, β) (9.1)
asks for all pairs (α, g) ∈ IsoFp(M, M′) × Γ satisfying αθ(q) = θ′(βg q)α (q ∈ Q). (9.2)"

With `M = M′ = F_p^a`, `compatPairs θ θ' β` is the set of `(α, g) ∈ GL(a, p) × Γ` with
`α θ(q) = θ′(β_g q) α` for all `q ∈ Q`. `compatPairs θ θ β` is the **source stabilizer**.

**Formalization Note.** Bases of `M` and `M′` are fixed, so `Iso_{F_p}(M, M′)` is `GL(a, p)`. The
homomorphism `β` need not be injective. -/
def compatPairs {p a k s : ℕ} {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {gens : Fin s → Equiv.Perm (Fin k)}
    (θ θ' : Q →* GL (Fin a) (ZMod p)) (β : ↥(gammaOf gens) →* MulAut Q) :
    Set (GL (Fin a) (ZMod p) × ↥(gammaOf gens)) :=
  {x | ∀ q : Q, x.1 * θ q = θ' (β x.2 q) * x.1}

end GroupIsoPoly


